The title only says faster IndexOf for substrings but tests and benchmarks are also for byte. Would that PR also improves the performance of IndexOf for `(ReadOnly)Span<byte>` ? I.e.:

```C#
byte[] b = new byte[1_000_000] { /* .... */  };
int index = b.AsSpan().IndexOf(0xC0);
```

> Would that PR also improves the performance of IndexOf
> int index = b.AsSpan().IndexOf(0xC0);

Your example searches for a single byte; this does not improve that. This does improve searching for a span of either multiple bytes or multiple chars.

